<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Our fork of LineageOS/android_device_qcom_sepolicy_vndr, for one fix.
  Only the legacy-um path is overridden; the sm8450/sm8550/sm8650/sm8750 paths
  belong to other devices and keep tracking upstream.

  WHY
  Building lineage-24.0 fails in precompiled_sepolicy:

    neverallow check failed at plat_sepolicy.cil:55562
      from system/sepolicy/private/pcc_component.te:366
      (neverallow pcc_component pcc_component
         (icmp_socket (ioctl read write create getattr setattr lock append map
         bind connect getopt setopt shutdown)))
      <root>
      allow at vendor_sepolicy.cil:12561
        from .../legacy/vendor/common/net.te:28
        (allow netdomain self:icmp_socket (...)))

  pcc_component is new in Android 17 - system/sepolicy/private/pcc_component.te
  does not exist in the 23.2 tree - and it calls net_domain(pcc_component) at
  line 10, so it carries the netdomain attribute and the legacy-um allow
  reached it. The offending allow is unchanged from 23.2; it was legal then,
  because the restriction did not exist.

  The fix narrows the rule rather than weakening policy. It keeps the permission
  for the other 51 netdomain domains and drops it only for the one domain the
  platform forbids. No exception is granted, no check is relaxed:

    allow { netdomain -pcc_component } self:icmp_socket create_socket_perms;

  Attribute subtraction in an allow source set is stock AOSP; see
  system/sepolicy/private/adbd_common.te:27.

  Nothing here needs the dropped grant: of 681 vendor blobs only libllvm-qcom.so
  and libllvm-glnext.so contain the string icmp at all and neither imports a
  socket, ping or icmp symbol, and the tree never instantiates pcc_component.

  NOT OUR REGRESSION. Upstream lineage-24.0-legacy-um at 33df3b661808 carries the
  same unfixed rule, so there is nothing to pull instead. secilc reports every
  neverallow violation in one pass and this was the only one in the tree.

  WHY remove-project, and why the name has no LineageOS/ prefix
  This project already exists in the upstream manifest at
  snippets/lineage.xml:83, and repo keeps one shared path table across the main
  manifest and every file in .repo/local_manifests/, so re-declaring the same
  path is rejected with "duplicate path". remove-project frees it first.

  The name omits the LineageOS/ prefix because repo composes the fetch URL as
  <remote fetch>/<project name>; keeping the prefix would ask for
  anton-scholten/LineageOS/android_device_qcom_sepolicy_vndr, which does not
  exist. The global insteadOf rule then rewrites https to ssh.

  TO DO: send a Gerrit change to LineageOS/android_device_qcom_sepolicy_vndr for
  the same one-liner. Once it lands, delete this file, run
  `repo sync -c device/qcom/sepolicy_vndr/legacy-um`, and the path goes back to
  tracking upstream on its own.
-->
<manifest>
  <remove-project name="LineageOS/android_device_qcom_sepolicy_vndr"
                  path="device/qcom/sepolicy_vndr/legacy-um" />

  <project path="device/qcom/sepolicy_vndr/legacy-um"
           name="android_device_qcom_sepolicy_vndr"
           remote="anton" revision="lineage-24.0" />
</manifest>